%description:
A UE measures cells on its primary carrier only, the first of its carrier list, and a base
station sends its beacon on its own primary carrier, the first of its list. A UE whose serving
cell lists the same carriers in another order therefore never measures its serving cell, and
with handover enabled it would compare every candidate against a serving-cell signal it never
measured.

The UE here is attached to gnb, which lists its carriers as 3.5 GHz and 2 GHz, while the UE
lists them as 2 GHz and 3.5 GHz, and has handover enabled. The first beacon of its serving cell
is an error that names the serving cell; the error of InterFrequencyHandoverRejected, which says
that the UE would never hand over to the cell, would be wrong here.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: test.ned
import simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork;

network ServingCellCarrierOrderTestNetwork extends NrSessionTestNetwork
{
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = ServingCellCarrierOrderTestNetwork

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 2
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].carrierFrequency = 3.5GHz
*.gnb.cellularNic.numCarriers = 2
*.gnb.cellularNic.phy.componentCarrierModules = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1] carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0]"
*.ue[*].cellularNic.nrPhy.componentCarrierModules = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0] carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1]"

*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[*].nrServingNodeId = 1
**.enableHandover = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
received the beacon of its serving cell 1 on 3.5 GHz, which is not its primary carrier (2 GHz)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
